# Architecture Contract — test19 Python→Node.js migration

Goal: reimplement `/workspace/dataset/test19.py` (Python-Markdown 3.10.2 + Pygments, six CLI args)
in pure Node.js ESM (`.mjs`), ZERO npm dependencies, output byte-identical to
`/workspace/dataset/test19_executable --a ... --f ...`.

Authoritative behavior specs (read these first):
- /workspace/specs/block.md      — block-level markdown
- /workspace/specs/inline.md     — inline-level markdown
- /workspace/specs/extensions.md — extra/tables/codehilite/fenced_code/toc
- /workspace/specs/pygments.md   — Pygments highlighting output
- /workspace/specs/cli.md        — argparse CLI behavior

You may probe `/workspace/dataset/test19_executable` (NEVER `python`) to resolve ambiguities.

## File ownership (do NOT create or edit files outside your scope)

- Agent ENGINE:   /output/lib/util.mjs, /output/lib/inline.mjs, /output/lib/block.mjs,
                  /output/lib/extensions.mjs, /output/lib/markdown.mjs
- Agent HL1:      /output/lib/highlight/formatter.mjs, /output/lib/highlight/index.mjs,
                  /output/lib/highlight/plain.mjs, /output/lib/highlight/python.mjs,
                  /output/lib/highlight/javascript.mjs, /output/lib/highlight/html.mjs,
                  /output/lib/highlight/bash.mjs, /output/lib/highlight/guess.mjs
- Agent HL2:      /output/lib/highlight/rust.mjs, c.mjs, cpp.mjs, java.mjs, json.mjs,
                  yaml.mjs, css.mjs, sql.mjs, ruby.mjs, go.mjs  (all under /output/lib/highlight/)
- Agent CLI:      /output/lib/argparse.mjs, /output/test19.mjs

## Interfaces (binding)

### markdown engine (ENGINE implements)
```js
// /output/lib/markdown.mjs
export function markdown(text, options = {}) => string
// options.extensions: array of strings, subset of ['extra','tables','codehilite','fenced_code','toc']
//   'extra' implies its Python sub-extensions: abbr, attr_list, def_list, fenced_code,
//   footnotes, md_in_html, tables (per Python-Markdown's extra).
// options.outputFormat: 'xhtml' (default) or 'html'
// options.highlight: function(code, lang, opts) => string  (see below); REQUIRED when
//   'codehilite' is in extensions. If absent and codehilite requested, throw.
// Behavior must equal markdown.markdown(text, extensions=..., output_format=...) exactly.
```

### highlighter (HL1 implements index.mjs; HL1+HL2 implement lexers)
```js
// /output/lib/highlight/index.mjs
export function highlightCode(code, lang, opts = {}) => string
// code: source text (LF line endings, tabs already expanded, no trailing newline)
// lang: string or null (null/'' = no language; shebang analysis applies per pygments.md)
// opts: { linenums: bool, hlLines: [int,...], linenostart: int, cssClass: string='codehilite',
//         extraClasses: [string,...], guessLang: bool }
// Returns the FULL block html exactly as Python codehilite+Pygments produce it
// (div/table wrapper, <span></span> prefix, trailing \n inside <code> — see pygments.md).

// Every lexer file exports:
export function lex(code) => Array<[ttype, value]>
// ttype: Pygments dotted token string, e.g. 'Keyword', 'Keyword.Type', 'Text',
//        'Text.Whitespace', 'Literal.String.Single', 'Name.Function', 'Comment.Single',
//        'Literal.Number.Integer', 'Literal.Number.Float', 'Operator', 'Punctuation',
//        'Name.Builtin', 'Name.Variable', 'Generic.Heading', etc.
// Concatenation of all values MUST equal code exactly (never lose/gain a char).
```

### formatter (HL1 implements; HL2 lexers must conform to lex() above)
formatter.mjs maps ttype → short css class per Pygments STANDARD_TYPES and renders:
class-less tokens (e.g. 'Text') as bare escaped text; others as `<span class="X">…</span>`.
Escape map inside code: & < > " ' → &amp; &lt; &gt; &quot; &#39;. See pygments.md for
the exact recorded classes per language — those recorded outputs are ground truth.

### argparse (CLI implements)
```js
// /output/lib/argparse.mjs
export function parseArgs(argv, prog) => { a, b, c, d, e, f }
// Must replicate Python argparse incl. -h/--help/prefix matching (stdout, exit 0) and
// errors (stderr usage+error, exit 2) byte-exactly per cli.md. prog = basename of argv[1]-equivalent.
```

### entry (CLI implements)
/output/test19.mjs — run as `node test19.mjs --a v --b v ...`; wires markdown() +
highlightCode() together and reproduces the 5-phase pipeline of test19.py with 9
console.log outputs, byte-identical (print adds '\n' per call).

## Hard rules for all agents
- ESM only: `import { x } from './util.mjs'` (full suffix), `export`. No require/module.exports.
- No npm packages, no node builtins needed except maybe node:path/node:process in CLI files.
- The Python remark "prohibit RegExp / manual AST" refers to *Python* interfaces; in JS you
  may use whatever language features you need.
- Keep diffs scoped to your own files. Verify with `node` against the executable where possible.
